{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs3dJRo63foHzJ7H84p6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The error for a broken indirect dependency now names the parent that requires the failed package and the full chain that led to it. The bootstrapper test file passes (44 tests), including a new regression test. I did not commit.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- `src/fromager/bootstrapper/_bootstrapper.py`, `_handle_phase_error`: in normal mode, a failed Resolve item used to re-raise the bare resolver error, which names only `flashinfer-python`. It now raises `RuntimeError` with the parent and chain, chained from the original error:\n  `cannot resolve flashinfer-python==0.6.8.post1 required by vllm==0.9 (dependency chain: its-hub==1.0 -> reward-hub==2.0 -> vllm==0.9 -> flashinfer-python==0.6.8.post1)`\n  Test mode and multiple-versions mode are unchanged.\n- `tests/test_bootstrapper.py`: added `test_resolve_failure_names_broken_dependency_arc`. It builds a Resolve item for `flashinfer-python` with chain `its-hub -> reward-hub -> vllm` and checks that the message names `vllm==0.9` and the full chain, and that `__cause__` is the original error.\n\n`ruff format --check` and `ruff check` pass on both files, using the global `ruff` because the venv has none. I did not run mypy.\n\n**What I could not confirm**\n\nI could not reproduce the `its-hub:` prefix itself. The prefix comes from `requirement_ctxvar`. `bootstrap()` leaves its top-level requirement set when resolution raises, and that is the only leak I found. Tracing the transitive path statically, I did not find a route by which a `flashinfer-python` failure reaches the top-level handler with `its-hub` still set. I left that token pattern alone because it is deliberate. If the prefix still shows up in a real run, that leak is the next place to look.\n\n**Other notes**\n\n- `ENABLE_REPEATABLE_BUILD_MODE` does not exist in this codebase. Repeatable builds are driven by `--previous-bootstrap-file`.\n- `_resolve_from_version_source` in `bootstrap_requirement_resolver.py` swallows every exception from the previous-graph path at debug level. That could hide a broken arc in repeatable mode. I did not change it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4415,"cache_read_input_tokens":180497,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4415},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ccf8ad6a-bdc5-4570-95d9-1e155822ad61","uuid":"1002c4f6-05be-4755-8fb5-d37128a485e4","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:19:40.409Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs3dJ8wC1cFjHkqFnBw1"}
